  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving Protection and Living Conditions and Reducing Vulnerabilities of Crisis-Affected Populations in North-East Nigeria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM has been at the forefront of the humanitarian response in North-East Nigeria since the beginning of the crisis. In an effort to alleviate the above-described challenges, IOM has been providing multi-sectoral assistance to internally displaced persons (IDPs), returnees and host communities, and an overall displacement and operating picture to tailor the humanitarian response. With the continuous inter-sectoral vulnerabilities and needs of people, IOM sees the need to continue to provide necessary assistance to the affected population. Activities are being implemented in displacement sites as well as host communities. Through this project, IOM is providing direct assistance pertaining to the following sectors: camp coordination and camp management; shelter and non-food items; water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH); and mental health and psychosocial support. Additionally, the Organization continues to provide inter-agency services through the maintenance and operation of humanitarian hubs, the implementation of the Displacement Tracking matrix (DTM). To support durable solutions for protracted displacement, IOM is providing necessary immediate shelter, WASH and livelihood support, while simultaneously assisting State and local government leadership with technical support on the key principles, approaches, displacement data and needs, and models of durable solutions programming.</narrative>
  </description>
